+## Loopback hardening addendum (2026-09-03)
+
+### Scope and compatibility
+
+- Backup ref `codex/backup-vda-loopback-e1f248d` preserves the exact pre-change
+  state `e1f248dab69aa0e3504d8249613a096e4030673d`. The isolated implementation
+  branch is `codex/vda-loopback-only`; code commit is `48b44e6`.
+- `ramic_bridge.il` now defaults `RBLocal` to `t`, so a newly loaded daemon
+  binds `127.0.0.1`. The existing monitor control is retained: a Bridge user
+  can still make an explicit non-local choice, but it is no longer the default.
+- `SSHRunner.start_port_forward` now uses the explicit local forward
+  `127.0.0.1:<local>:127.0.0.1:<remote>` plus `GatewayPorts=no`. Hidden-window,
+  jump-host, state-file, retry, and cleanup behavior are unchanged.
+- `daemon_guard.py` queries the daemon-reported `RBLastBind`; `bridge status`
+  prints it and returns failure when a responsive daemon is non-loopback or
+  cannot provide bind evidence. The wire protocol and arbitrary SKILL
+  capability were not changed.
+- VDA adds its own stricter fail-closed check before every RAMIC-backed OA or
+  compute operation. VDA does not expose a bypass for non-loopback listeners.
+
