+
+### Security boundary
+
+Loopback binding closes the administrator-reported external-network exposure.
+It does not add application-layer authentication between Unix users already on
+the same multi-user server. Stronger per-user isolation would require a
+separate, protocol-changing design such as an authenticated channel or a
+permissioned Unix-domain socket and is intentionally not hidden inside this
+compatibility patch. Native Cadence listeners are also outside this patch and
+must be assessed by the server administrator or Cadence guidance.
+
+### Upstream upgrade addition
+
+After the four transport commits listed above, cherry-pick `48b44e6` only if
+the new upstream still defaults RAMIC or local forwarding to a wildcard
+address, or lacks actual-bind reporting. Re-run the 100 Bridge tests, VDA
+tests, remote `ss` checks, a CIW-attached read-only SKILL probe, and process
+cleanup checks before retiring `codex/backup-vda-loopback-e1f248d`.
