+## Windows SSH request-framing addendum (2026-09-04)
+
+### Trigger and bounded diagnosis
+
+- After the loopback daemon was loaded in a fresh headless IC6.1.8 session,
+  server-local TCP returned the standard `STX + 3` response for `1+2`.
+- The same request through Windows OpenSSH returned an empty response both with
+  explicit `-L 127.0.0.1:65347:127.0.0.1:65346` and with the legacy omitted
+  local bind address. Both tunnels still used `GatewayPorts=no` and were
+  verified to listen only on local loopback.
+- The failing client called `shutdown(SHUT_WR)` after sending JSON. On this
+  current Windows OpenSSH path the forwarded channel could be closed before the
+  daemon reply returned. The A/B excludes loopback binding itself as the cause.
+
+### Exact changes and compatibility
+
+1. `src/virtuoso_bridge/virtuoso/basic/bridge.py`
+   - A Windows client with an SSH tunnel keeps its write side open while waiting
+     for the reply.
+   - Local-mode Windows and all non-Windows paths retain the legacy half-close,
+     minimizing compatibility impact with an older daemon.
+2. `ramic_bridge_daemon_3.py` and `ramic_bridge_daemon_27.py`
+   - Each daemon parses and dispatches as soon as one complete JSON value has
+     arrived instead of requiring EOF.
+   - Fragmented TCP and UTF-8 input is accumulated until complete. EOF and
+     malformed-input error behavior remain available for legacy clients.
+3. Tests
+   - `test_daemon_request_framing.py` loads the actual parser functions from
+     both standalone daemon resources and verifies fragmented UTF-8 JSON without
+     EOF plus malformed legacy EOF.
+   - `test_virtuoso_tunnel_recovery.py` proves Windows tunneled requests do not
+     half-close and that the legacy path still does.
+   - `test_runtime_paths.py` now sets `USERPROFILE` together with `HOME` in its
+     Windows legacy-cache fixture; runtime path behavior was not changed.
+
+The modified Windows client must be paired with a freshly deployed/reloaded
+daemon. A stale old daemon can still wait for EOF; the supported upgrade path
+is `virtuoso-bridge start` followed by reloading its generated setup. The new
+daemon remains compatible with clients that still half-close. No SKILL body,
+return marker, authentication, OA, Spectre, retry, or replay semantics changed.
+
+### Recovery points and verification
+
+- Backup ref `codex/backup-vda-framing-afd7346` preserves exact pre-change
+  commit `afd7346`; implementation commit is `b1194ca` on the unpushed private
+  branch `codex/vda-loopback-only`.
+- Framing/tunnel targeted suite: `11 passed`.
+- Full Bridge suite in an isolated cwd, empty test `.env`, and explicit
+  basetemp: `106 passed`.
+- Full VDA suite: `910 passed`.
+- Two obsolete headless Virtuoso sessions dating from 2026-07-05 were verified
+  by UID, executable, cwd, restore file, parent tree, and DISPLAY, then exited
+  normally after SIGTERM. No force kill or file deletion was needed.
+- One replacement session loaded the uploaded setup from
+  `/data/xum/virtuoso_bridge_xum/Aurora_s_Echo/virtuoso_bridge`. Remote `ss` and
+  the CIW log both reported `127.0.0.1:65346`.
+- Final Windows-tunnel `1+2` returned `3`; VDA doctor returned
+  `connected=true`, `skill_probe=3`, `daemon_bind=127.0.0.1:65346`, and profile
+  `nics4304_tsmc28`.
+- This smoke did not open, read, or write OA and did not run a Spectre analysis.
+
+### Upstream upgrade addition
+
+After applying the loopback patch, cherry-pick `b1194ca` only if upstream still
