+and `test_runtime_paths`. New `test_vda_upgrade_compatibility.py` checks the
+bind policy, workspace token provisioning/unsafe path rejection, and fragmented
+signed responses including tampering. Fixture changes isolate site env/owner
+checks, preserve upstream lazy construction, and account for complete-JSON
+dispatch; they do not suppress real security or execution failures.
+
+### Reconciled rather than copied
+
+Upstream's native Windows process-liveness checks, stale state/target cache,
+default daemon loopback, signed capabilities/owner checks, IPC resynchronization,
+bounded Busy handling and durable recovery implementation are retained. The old
+extra USER-query retry is superseded by signed owner identity/cache; it is not
+layered on top as an additional SKILL replay. `VirtuosoClient.from_env()` keeps
+upstream's lazy no-tunnel construction (including daemon-independent docs use);
+the first actual EDA request acquires auth and may perform the same safe
+pre-send warm recovery. No post-send reset/timeout may rebuild and replay SKILL.
+The explicit shared-CIW guard's `retry_connect=False` remains respected.
+
+During live acceptance, a native Windows forward delivered a valid full signed
+hello but not EOF. The client now finishes receiving only after verification of
+the MAC over the entire accumulated body and that request's nonce. Partial or
+tampered replies still fail. This is not the old unsigned legacy fallback;
+production authentication remains enabled and no signature check is skipped.
+
+### Verified boundaries
+
+- Untouched upstream on proper Linux/POSIX temp storage: 2,286 passed,
+  89 skipped. Integrated final Linux suite: 2,325 passed, 89 skipped.
+- Final private/core Windows set: 165 passed, 2 skipped. Full native Windows
+  runs retain upstream's separately recorded platform failures; see VDA's
+  dated upgrade record for exact baseline/final counts and failure-set diff.
