+  initially hit a pre-existing Windows temp-directory ACL issue; an explicit
+  isolated basetemp passes without modifying tests or system permissions.
+- Read-only OA-to-si-to-Spectre TSMC18 DC/AC on the existing common-source cell:
+  identical netlist SHA-256 and all 28 raw metrics versus the previous run;
+  gain 20.826709 dB, BW 125.833557 MHz, power 68.322394 uW. The two-variant
+  TSMC N28 standalone AC preview also passes with parsed PSF evidence.
+- Both original interactive Virtuoso processes were preserved. The selected
+  existing PID 94710 was upgraded in place without OA writes; the new signed
+  handshake identifies that same PID. Actual daemon bind is loopback and
+  VDA doctor works for both profiles. The old 0.8 wire required an isolated
+  one-time adapter accepting only independently known exact read-only owner/
+  PID/bind replies before a single public Bridge reload request; it is not
+  part of production source or an auth-disabled fallback.
+- An owned headless test session and all its verified process groups were
+  stopped. One-shot UI migration loaders were retired to no-ops after keeping
+  audit originals, preventing delayed UI input from restarting anything.
+  Temporary ports are not the final default. User `cds.lib` hash is unchanged.
+
+This is a dependency/execution compatibility Gate, not new PVT, layout, SOS,
+Maestro GUI, arbitrary parameter-write or L5B design-quality validation.
+
+## 2026-10-18 focused feature acceptance follow-up
+
+Before this follow-up, `codex/backup-pre-feature-validation-20261018` was created
+at `e214d3a6e153a036d422b5453412365b8172cd06`. The verified post-upgrade bundle
+and original venv/source backups remain available in VDA's ignored artifacts.
+Changes stay on `codex/vda-upstream-main-20261018`; do not push to third-party origin.
+
+### Exact additional delta
+
+- `virtuoso/basic/bridge.py`: skip `SHUT_WR` for all Windows clients, not just
+  managed-tunnel instances. A native Windows socketpair reproduced reply loss
+  after half-close independently of SSH. Receipt-only direct clients need the
+  same complete-JSON framing. POSIX retains half-close. No post-send retry added.
+- `tools/skill_exec.py`: use the same Windows request framing and only finish
+  early when the entire response verifies against the request nonce/HMAC;
+  carry one monotonic deadline through receiving. Authentication stays enabled.
+- `test_daemon_auth.py` and `test_recoverable_daemon.py`: fake/raw clients follow
+  the paired daemon's complete-JSON protocol; Windows fixtures no longer require
+  half-close. Security assertions remain intact.
+- `test_vda_upgrade_compatibility.py` and `test_virtuoso_tunnel_recovery.py`:
+  cover Windows direct and standalone signed fragmented responses, rejection of
+  tampering, and retained POSIX behavior. `test_request_recovery_transport.py`
+  adds diagnostics to the existing pending-receipt assertion, without relaxing it.
+
+### Evidence and remaining boundaries
+
+- Focused Linux auth/recovery/framing/reader suite: 281 passed, 2 skipped.
+  Final private compatibility/platform matrix: 29 passed.
+- Final focused Windows deterministic private/recovery/framing set: 96 passed.
+  Broader localhost TCP set: 271 passed, 3 failed, 6 skipped; intermittent
+  `WinError 10054` remains in negative capability, explicit auth-off, and busy
+  transport tests. No repeated-to-green acceptance or claim of all-Windows success.
+- VDA full suite: 936 passed, including the seven new opt-in parameter-evidence
+  contract tests. The compact reader and old task approval token remain unchanged.
+- On an isolated owned Virtuoso session, an injected lost acknowledgement was
+  reconciled through the original receipt after replacing only the local tunnel;
+  both submission count and SKILL counter were exactly one. A real client budget
+  exhaustion during an 8-second SKILL sleep likewise recovered the original
+  completion with counter one. Its guard phase was indeterminate/awaiting_user,
+  not evidence that every timeout or dialog branch is covered.
+- Rich stored/CDF evidence was read live without changing compact values. VDA
+  integration and OA/si binding results, timings, owned process cleanup, and
+  failed first-use PDK/session attempts are recorded in VDA's
+  `docs/validation/2026-10-18-bridge-feature-workflow.md`.
